        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:18%;">De-esc 18%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> IRGC's formal Hormuz closure declaration and the IAEA non-compliance ruling, absent a confirmed negotiating session, sustain the blockade into a fourth month and leave Iranian hardliners with procedural cover to break off diplomatic channels entirely.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Back-channel activity at named-principal level (Araghchi-Thawadi) and the G7 Evian window maintain diplomatic momentum without producing a formally convened session, holding the conflict in a frozen-but-active state with Hormuz closed and no new direct bilateral exchanges.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> A formal US-Iran framework is signed at or immediately after G7 Evian (June 15–17), activating the 15-nation MCM coalition and reducing acute escalation risk as Hormuz reopening preparations begin.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>

      <p>Iranian state media on June 11–12 ran on two parallel tracks. IRNA's lead coverage framed Trump's cancellation of strikes as a product of Iranian "resistance": the IRGC's joint military command issued a statement through Tasnim claiming its "resistance and heavy fire" in the strait had left US forces "shocked," an account CENTCOM did not corroborate — no US warships were reported hit. Tasnim, the IRGC-affiliated outlet, responded to Trump's deal announcement by stating his words "cannot be taken at face value unless Iran officially announces an agreement," a formulation that simultaneously denies Trump credit while keeping the door procedurally open. → supports <span class="cite">F1</span> without move</p>

      <p>Kayhan, the hardline daily closest to the Office of the Supreme Leader, ran front-page commentary on the IAEA non-compliance ruling as an act of "political warfare" by Western states, arguing the Board vote was "illegal" because it occurred under conditions of active foreign military aggression against Iran. Press TV amplified the IRGC's June 11 formal closure declaration as a sovereign act of self-defense, not an escalation. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>

      <p>The internal framing division is notable: IRNA and MFA-aligned outlets (Baghaei's "no final decision" formulation) maintained procedural neutrality toward a potential deal; IRGC-aligned outlets (Tasnim, Kayhan) ran harder resistance rhetoric. Araghchi's overnight engagement with the Qatari envoy was absent from Iranian state media as of the morning of June 12 — a consistent pattern of the regime conducting diplomacy without public attribution. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

